दुरूह a. difficult to be perceived or understood;
 abstr.
˚त्व n.

दुर्ग॑ a. hard to go through or to, difficult of access or
attainment, impassable, unaccessible. m. N. of an Asura & sev. men;
 n.
rough ground, difficult place;
 mountain, hill, crag, stronghold, castle;
difficulty, danger, distress;
 f. आ N. of a goddess, the daughter of
Himavant and wife of Śiva.

2 दुर्ग्रह m. stubbornness, a foolish whim;
 an evil demon
(causing diseases).

दुर्जय a. difficult to be subdued or overcome,
invincible;
 m. N. of a Dānava, a Rakṣas, & sev. men.

दुर्ध॑र a. hard to be borne, held, restrained,
administered (punishment), kept in mind or recollected;
 m. a man's name.

दुर्धर्ष a. difficult to be assaulted or approached,
invincible, dangerous, terrible;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

दुर्बल a. weak, feeble, thin, unwell;
 poor, scanty.
Abstr. ˚ता f.

दुर्भ॑ग a. uncomfortable, unpleasant, unhappy;
 abstr.
˚त्व† n.

2 दुर्म॑द a. drunken, fierce, extravagant;
 very fond of,
all eager for (—˚).

दुर्म॑र्ष a. not to be forgotten, imperishable;
 also =
seq.

दुर्मित्र॑ a. unfriendly, inimical (also ˚त्रिय॑);
 m. a
man's name.

दुर्मुख f. ई having an ugly face or a foul mouth;
 m. a
man's name.

दु॑र्य a. belonging to the door or house;
 m. & f. आ pl.
residence, home.

दुर्योधन a. difficult to be conquered, invincible
(abstr. ˚ता f.);
 m. N. of the eldest son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.

दुर्लभ a. difficult to be obtained or seen;
 rare,
precious dear;
 difficult i.g. (w. infin.).

दुर्ललित a. fondled too much, ill-bred;
 n. ill
behaviour, a roguish trick.

दुर्वाच्य a. hard to be uttered, harsh (words);
 n. harsh
language or bad news.

दूरत॑स् adv. from afar, far away, far, not at hand;
 w.
भू keep in distance.

दूरी@कृ leave behind, remove, reject;
 w. भू go back,
retire, be far.
